{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"# Independent review of unmelted-cosmic-eeve\n\nReviewed revision: `d0081fc8b21d041aff94615c694ac0a50104f833`\n\nImmutable before revision: `0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e`\n\nReviewer session: `astatine-bigboned-mite` (`72d0-8a25-3a14-4d97`)\n\nAuthor session: `vapourific-voracious-nerka` (`59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148`)\n\nThe reviewer did not author or modify this revision. The shared Git and tracker service principal is `RebarBotNava <joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com>`. Session-level provenance distinguishes the author and reviewer.\n## Review summary\n\nStage 1 (Spec Compliance): FAIL\n\nArchitecture Compliance: PASS. The normalized executable AST is unchanged, so the patch does not alter architecture or a user-visible vertical slice.\n\nStage 2 (Code Quality): NOT RUN. Stage 1 failure blocks later stages.\n\nStage 3 (Domain Integrity): NOT RUN. Stage 1 failure blocks later stages. The normalized AST proof independently establishes that no runtime domain types or state representations changed.\n\nOverall: CHANGES REQUIRED\n\nThe exact path set, normalized AST, directive-bearing physical lines, protected prose, and inline comments are unchanged outside the 30 selected blocks. All 30 selected blocks preserve their scoped contracts and strictly shrink. Focused tests passed with 71 tests. Path-scoped diff integrity and comment hygiene passed. Full local verification was omitted under the operator's documentation-only CI waiver.\n\n### Blocking findings\n\n1. IMPORTANT. Thirteen edited blocks use clause-joining semicolons forbidden by `docs/documentation-policy.md`. Locations are `tests/interfaces/conftest.py:72`, `tests/interfaces/conftest.py:76`, `tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py:217`, `tests/interfaces/test_write_parity_oracle.py:6`, `tests/interfaces/test_write_parity_oracle.py:35`, `tests/interfaces/write_parity_contract.py:6`, `tests/interfaces/write_parity_contract.py:23`, `tests/interfaces/write_parity_contract.py:32`, `tests/interfaces/write_parity_contract.py:45`, `tests/interfaces/write_parity_contract.py:99`, `tests/interfaces/write_parity_contract.py:181`, `tests/interfaces/write_parity_contract.py:221`, and `tests/interfaces/write_parity_contract.py:255`.\n2. IMPORTANT. The edited docstring at `tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py:126` uses undated `today's`, which the same policy bans when it adds current-value emphasis.\n\nRequired changes:\n\n1. Replace each clause-joining semicolon with policy-compliant sentences or conjunctions while retaining strict shrinkage and meaning.\n2. Replace `today's known pointer list` with a current-state phrase such as `the known pointer list`.\n3. Amend the same Gerrit Change-Id and request a fresh exact-SHA independent review.\n\n## Exact block receipt\n\n```tsv\npath/block\tbefore\tfinal\tpreserved-contract-or-consumer\tbefore-words\tafter-words\tsemantic-preservation\tbloat-removal\treviewer-session\ntests/interfaces/conftest.py#comment:_rebar_repo_template:tracker-branch\t0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e:tests/interfaces/conftest.py:L90\td0081fc8b21d041aff94615c694ac0a50104f833:tests/interfaces/conftest.py:L82\tTracker creation is proven on the tickets branch.\t9\t7\tPASS\tPASS\t72d0-8a25-3a14-4d97\ntests/interfaces/conftest.py#comment:_rebar_repo_template:ticket-free\t0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e:tests/interfaces/conftest.py:L76\td0081fc8b21d041aff94615c694ac0a50104f833:tests/interfaces/conftest.py:L75\tConstruction keeps the template ticket-free and protects narrowed-suite emptiness consumers.\t108\t29\tPASS\tPASS\t72d0-8a25-3a14-4d97\ntests/interfaces/conftest.py#comment:_rebar_repo_template:no-rebar-state\t0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e:test